  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Which of the following conditions is insufficient to conclude that quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) is a parallelogram?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(AB\\parallel CD\\), \\(AD\\parallel BC\\)",
    "B": "\\(AB=CD\\), \\(AD=BC\\)",
    "C": "\\(AB\\parallel CD\\), \\(AD=BC\\)",
    "D": "\\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\) bisect each other."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "One pair of opposite sides being parallel and the other pair being equal is insufficient to conclude that a quadrilateral is a parallelogram. An isosceles trapezoid is a counterexample. The other three options are all criteria for identifying a parallelogram.",
